  "description": "Luxibel Aurora Blast: tilt-only (no pan) IP wash with a wide rectangular lens tray between two flat side cheeks on a box base with LCD + 4 buttons. Tray (counted in photos 3/4/1): upper tier 5 (top row, right slot empty) + 6, a clear-tube cool-white strobe bar across the middle (144 LEDs, 12 segments per spec), lower tier 6 + 5 (bottom row, left slot empty) = 22 x 40W RGBW cells, aligned columns (not staggered). Spec: 410 x 520 x 201 mm, 23.1 kg, tilt 200 deg, zoom 4-45 deg. Earlier pass text follows: This is probably a Luxibel Aurora Blast, a single moving-head wash fixture with a wide rectangular housing, roughly 52 by 45 by 30 cm. A small-footed base sits on the floor and carries a yoke that holds the head. The front of the head is a rectangular lens tray with rounded corners, and a carry handle sits at its top right rear. The optic is an array of 22 round domed cells: an upper tier of two rows, a horizontal LED pixel strip across the middle, and a lower tier of two staggered rows, giving 22 independently controllable RGBW cells. The head tilts on one axis through a total range of about 200 degrees, probably, with the base fixed and no pan. Ribbed vent slots run along the lower front shell, and an LCD display with four buttons sits on the lower rear as a fixed control panel.",
